DOS-PORT (patch 0102, Phase 10 Stage 3). Concrete MidiBackend
implementation routing MIDI events to WaveBlaster header /
DreamBlaster S2 daughterboard via SDL/0037+'s MPU-401 helpers
(SDL_DOSMpu401* family at vendor/SDL/src/core/dos/SDL_dos_audio_synth.h).

Selected when SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_AUDIO_BACKEND=wb. SoundManager::init()
probes via SDL_DOSMpu401Init at the port returned by
SDL_DOSMpu401GetBLASTERPort (parses BLASTER env var Pxxxx field;
defaults to 0x330 — canonical MPU-401 port shared with most SB16-class
hardware including the g2k Vibra16S CT2490). On probe success:
MidiBackendWaveBlaster installed on singleton MidiScheduler. On probe
failure: log + roll g_p10_audio_backend_active back to organya so the
engine's existing Organya music-dispatch path takes over. Pixtone SFX
unaffected either way.

NEW files (2):

  src/sound/MidiBackendWB.{h,cpp} — MidiBackendWaveBlaster class.
    Constructor: probe MPU-401 + set _ready flag (used by
    SoundManager::init to decide install-or-fallback).
    note_on / note_off / control_change: 3-byte MIDI message via
    _send3() helper (defensive 7-bit data-byte masking).
    program_change: 2-byte (status + program) — special case since
    program-change is the only single-data-byte MIDI message.
    on_song_start / on_song_stop: All-Notes-Off (CC 123) + All-Sound-Off
    (CC 120) on every channel — prevents stuck notes across song
    boundaries (the loop-from-start semantic in MidiScheduler can
    re-dispatch on top of a still-sustaining note from the prior
    iteration). Both CCs sent for hardware-quirk robustness (some
    GM synths handle 120 better; some 123).
    Destructor: All-Notes-Off + SDL_DOSMpu401Shutdown.

MODIFIED (2):

  src/sound/AudioBackend.cpp — selectBackendFromEnv handles "wb" env
    value: sets g_p10_audio_backend_active = wb (slot-0100 fallback
    "Stage 3 not yet shipped" retired). Runtime probe + fallback
    happens in SoundManager::init.

  src/sound/SoundManager.cpp — three integration points:
    1. init(): when backend==wb, instantiate MidiBackendWaveBlaster
       (probes in constructor); if isReady(), install on MidiScheduler;
       else log "WB backend probe failed; falling back to organya"
       and update g_p10_audio_backend_active back to organya. The
       wb-fallback IS a backend swap per PHASE10-CONTRACT.md § 1.2's
       anticipated case.
    2. music() / enableMusic(): midi_path predicate extended to also
       match wb (in addition to slot-0101's midi_stub). The runtime
       fallback path means wb only stays as the active enum here if
       MPU-401 hardware is responding.
    3. runFade(): MidiScheduler::tick driver predicate extended to
       include wb. Same pattern.

Smoke (DOSBox-X-fast, 3 gates per team-lead 2026-05-06 dispatch):

  Gate 1 — AUDIO_BACKEND=wb:
    DOSBox-X 2025.02 emulates MPU-401 (better than expected); probe
    SUCCEEDED at port 0x0330. MidiScheduler armed with
    MidiBackendWaveBlaster. MIDI parser loaded curly.mid (5684 events
    at 480 PPQ). MidiBackendWaveBlaster::on_song_start fired (sent
    All-Notes-Off + All-Sound-Off on all 16 channels followed by the
    .mid's own program_change events as MidiScheduler::tick
    dispatched them). 72 flips, no crashes/hangs/fatal markers.
    Engine ran the full WB hardware path end-to-end under emulation
    rather than the fallback path team-lead anticipated. Real
    operator iter on g2k will hear actual MIDI playback through the
    DreamBlaster S2 daughterboard for the first time when this
    iter runs.

  Gate 2 — AUDIO_BACKEND=organya regression:
    `audio backend: organya (forced; Phase 10 baseline)` logged;
    no MidiScheduler / wb backend involvement; 42 flips, no crashes.
    Default Organya path unchanged.

  Gate 3 — AUDIO_BACKEND=midi-stub regression:
    Stage 2 path still works; `MidiScheduler armed with
    MidiBackendStub` logged; 42 flips, no crashes.

